About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

Our Organization, Performance &amp; Change practice are looking for Summer Interns to join the team.

The Internship

This is an eight-week summer internship designed to give you a real look at consulting - not from the sidelines, but by getting close to the work.&nbsp; &nbsp;

You’ll&nbsp;join our&nbsp; Organization, Performance &amp; Change&nbsp; practice&nbsp;(OPC). We help clients answer questions like: How should teams be organized?&nbsp;How can I create lasting value in my organization?&nbsp;What needs to change for a strategy to work in real life? How do leaders bring people along? How can organizations build the culture,&nbsp;capabilities&nbsp;and ways of working they need for the future? &nbsp;

These questions have&nbsp;various answers and approaches,&nbsp;and each&nbsp;project is built&nbsp;with our client and their needs in mind.&nbsp;In practice, that means your work could look different from week to week. &nbsp;

You might… &nbsp;

• break down a complicated business problem and turn it into a clear story that helps a client decide where to invest for the future. &nbsp;

• help organizations navigate big changes - launching a new strategy, shifting how teams work or improving the employee experience. &nbsp;

• look at how companies are organized, how decisions get made, and how people work together across teams. &nbsp;

• map a “day in the life” for employees, identifying the moments that matter most. &nbsp;

• help find better, simpler ways for work to get done - from improving processes to making teams more effective. &nbsp;

• analyse complex datasets to generate insights that inform decisions made by both Baringa and our clients. &nbsp;

• help a client to optimize their cost base to deliver long-term savings.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• think about the people side of business, including leadership, culture, learning, talent and what helps people perform at their best. &nbsp;

• join complex team discussions where priorities shift, ideas evolve and collaboration matters. &nbsp;

So, what are we looking for?

We’re not expecting you to have consulting figured out already. We’re looking for students who are curious about how businesses work, energized by solving problems with others and excited to learn in a fast-moving, team-based environment. You’ll stand out if you bring: &nbsp;

• Curiosity about people,&nbsp;business&nbsp;and change &nbsp;- You like asking good questions and understanding what makes organizations work. &nbsp;
